nvenc_drv.h (NVIDIA, SPDX MIT, "1993-2023") and clc5b7.h (NVIDIA, MIT): NVENC's picture-setup structures and class
methods from NVIDIA's open-gpu-doc (github.com/NVIDIA/open-gpu-doc, classes/video/, commit 9fdf5c40 2026-06-09).
Unmodified. nvenc_drv.h is written for class C9B7 but keeps one layout for every NVENC from MSENC on: its magic table
lists NV_NVENC_5_0 = 0xd0b70006 (T210's NVENC 5.0 firmware holds exactly that value) with the same revision byte as
every later class. The methods TegraNVENC uses have the same offsets in clc5b7.h, clc7b7.h and clc9b7.h. Struct sizes
match the header's own comments under clang (512-byte H.264 picture setup); test/nvenc_host checks them.
Used by TegraNVENCCheck.h and SwitchVideoEncoders/AVE.
